# G17: the cross-reference graph draws the call neighbourhood of the selected function. Go to main in
# the debuggee (its entry, 0x1380). One call out, main has five functions in its graph and four calls
# among them; two calls out, eleven and eleven. Both numbers are the CLI's own call graph walked the
# same way (donkey-cli callgraph --json), not a second copy of the rule.
wait_idle
frames 5
assert_no_error

key g
text main
key enter
frames 3
assert_xref_graph 5 4
assert_xref_graph_has main
assert_xref_graph_has donkey_debuggee_tick

xref_depth 2
frames 2
assert_xref_graph 11 11
# The Xrefs window names the function that contains each end of a reference (G10-T4): the call at
# 0x1442 is inside main, and its target 0x11e9 is donkey_debuggee_tick.
assert_function_containing 0x1442 main
assert_function_containing 0x11e9 donkey_debuggee_tick
assert_no_error
